What is `n` if the code plants without writing `1` back into `bed`?

```java
int[] bed = {0, 0, 0};
int n = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < bed.length; i++) {
    boolean left = i == 0 || bed[i - 1] == 0;
    boolean right = i == bed.length - 1 || bed[i + 1] == 0;
    if (bed[i] == 0 && left && right) n++;
}
```

What is `n` after planting and marking each planted plot?

```java
int[] bed = {0, 0, 0};
int n = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < bed.length; i++) {
    boolean left = i == 0 || bed[i - 1] == 0;
    boolean right = i == bed.length - 1 || bed[i + 1] == 0;
    if (bed[i] == 0 && left && right) {
        bed[i] = 1;
        n++;
    }
}
```
